            "review_title": "Review at Cari Cua 63",
            "review_text": "Little Daisy77\nFreehold, New Jersey44 contributions\n0\nOrder with Caution!\nMay 2019 • Friends\nOur friend invited us to this restaurant and he highly recommend us to try curry crabs so we did order two crabs. They have two kinds of crabs 1) with string the price is a lot cheaper, but you end up paying more because the fabric they use to tie the crabs is pretty heavy due to water retention. 2) craby without string is about $300k vnd more than with string. The curry crabs flavors is really good and other snail dishes too. We went back here the next day without our friend and they don’t treat us the same because we are not locals. They know we are visitors so they give us not so good quality crabs. We complain to the waitress and she told us that the crab are not good today. They should have told us that when we place the order not wait until\nWe complain about it. So if you are foreigner or not the locals make sure to ask if the crabs are good or not. If they tell you it’s good then tell them if the crabs comes out bad you will return it. This way they won’t dare to give you bad ones. Enjoy 😉\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten May 26, 2019",
